    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n79818" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάροχος</span></b>  (B), ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρέχω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>provider</i>, c. gen., <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				2.12
			</span></i> (pl.) : 
				gloss on 
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόξενος</span>
			, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				182
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π., οἱ</span>, in
			the Roman provinces, <i>those who supplied public officers</i>
			with necessaries, Hor.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Sat.</u>
				1.5.46
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(1).209.30
			</span></i> (Sparta, <span class="entity">i B.C.</span>) : metaph., <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				13.2a
			</span></i>.<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>.</div>
